PURPOSE
  How Hydra engineers connect in to do remote PLC/SCADA work for WWP without
  being on site. Keep this current; WWP IT audits vendor access quarterly.

ACCESS PATH (how we get to the engineering workstation)
  1. Open a ticket with WWP IT (Dana Whitfield). IT enables our access to the
     OT jump host for the maintenance window. Players, note: there is no direct
     route from the corporate/IT network to the SCADA VLAN -- everything hops
     the jump host.
  2. Hop from the jump host to the engineering workstation over SSH:
         jump:  ssh eng
     (the ~/.ssh/config on the jump host has an "eng" alias; we authenticate
      with the hydra_vendor engineering key, not a password.)
  3. The engineering workstation (ww-eng01, {{ ww_net }}.40.20) is the only
     box permitted to reach the field controllers on tcp/502 and tcp/20256.

WHAT WE RUN ON THE ENGINEERING WORKSTATION
  - Toolkit lives in /opt/hydra-tools (world readable):
        pcom_client.py   Unitronics PCOM/TCP (V570 chem-feed, tcp/20256)
        mbtool.py        Modbus/TCP for all three controllers (tcp/502)
        tagmon.py        live tag monitor
    See /opt/hydra-tools/README.md for usage. The V570 commissioning note and
    its RUN/STOP control are PCOM-only -- Modbus won't reach them.
  - PLC project files are under ~m.oyelaran/projects (M340 intake, V570 chem
    feed, SCADAPack RTU03). Always snapshot before editing a live program.
  - Controllers by address:
        {{ ww_net }}.50.10   ww-plc01  Cedar River Intake PS-1 (M340)
        {{ ww_net }}.50.20   ww-plc02  WTP Chemical Feed (V570, Modbus + PCOM)
        {{ ww_net }}.50.30   ww-rtu03  Hilltop Booster PS-3 (SCADAPack 474)

OPERATOR / HMI SUPPORT
  For operator-facing issues we support the AquaView HMI at {{ ww_net }}.40.10:
    - web console over the jump host, and
    - VNC (:5900) via the jump host for screen-share with the control room.
  The control-room operators use the shared "controlroom" login on the HMI;
  get the current password from Priya Raman (control room lead) during the
  window -- do NOT store operator credentials in this runbook.

HOUSEKEEPING
  - Log every change in the project git repo with a clear message.
  - Return all protective settings to engineered values before leaving
    (especially RTU03 FCV-301 slew / SAV-301 after any surge test).
  - Close the ticket so IT can disable the jump-host access again.

